    {
      "id": "7rF7msbwnBL8Sf4mJOtva",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 528,
      "y": 128,
      "width": 774.6198120117188,
      "height": 825,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 938191633,
      "version": 1075,
      "versionNonce": 959538687,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1741655745750,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Functional Requirements: \n\n1. Metric and monitoring.\n2. capture metric of debug. -> success , failure, etc.\n3. query -> we want to find the metric between date range.\n\n\nNon-Functional Requirements: \n1.  Near real time. \n2. Accurate. \n3. query -> low latency. \n4. Available. -> its okok bit late  , need to be available.\n5. at max 90 of data -> remaining delete or store s3 cheap.\n\n\nEstimations:\n\n1. QPS -> 1B requests / seconds. \n2. Storage -> 2kb  -> per second -> 2 TB / second -> 2 * 10^5 tb / day\nFor storage 90 -> 18 * 10^5 TB day.\n\n\nHigh Level Design: \n\n\nApproach: \n        Error -> either can be like logger -> indirectly generating the events. \n                   basically -> out service will be calling this library. there is error. \n\n        Library -> api -> pushing events to pipeline. -> near real time. \n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Functional Requirements: \n\n1. Metric and monitoring.\n2. capture metric of debug. -> success , failure, etc.\n3. query -> we want to find the metric between date range.\n\n\nNon-Functional Requirements: \n1.  Near real time. \n2. Accurate. \n3. query -> low latency. \n4. Available. -> its okok bit late  , need to be available.\n5. at max 90 of data -> remaining delete or store s3 cheap.\n\n\nEstimations:\n\n1. QPS -> 1B requests / seconds. \n2. Storage -> 2kb  -> per second -> 2 TB / second -> 2 * 10^5 tb / day\nFor storage 90 -> 18 * 10^5 TB day.\n\n\nHigh Level Design: \n\n\nApproach: \n        Error -> either can be like logger -> indirectly generating the events. \n                   basically -> out service will be calling this library. there is error. \n\n        Library -> api -> pushing events to pipeline. -> near real time. \n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
